    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Seven chords in C major",
      "body": "Stack a diatonic triad on each degree of C major and you get C, D minor, E minor, F, G, A minor and B diminished. The pattern is always **major, minor, minor, major, major, minor, diminished**, in every major key.\n\n**Why it matters:** learn this one pattern and you know the seven chords of all twelve major keys.",
